{"id": "EUVD-2026-47879", "enisaUuid": "07414883-69d1-3d0e-98ed-9d9dbdc9ee44", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nxfs: resample the data fork mapping after cycling ILOCK\n\nxfs_reflink_fill_{cow_hole,delalloc} are both presented with an inode,\na data fork mapping, and a cow fork mapping.  Unfortunately, these two\nhelpers cycle the ILOCK to grab a transaction, which means that the\nmappings are stale as soon as we reacquire the ILOCK.  Currently we\nrefresh the cow fork mapping by re-calling xfs_find_trim_cow_extent, but\nwe don't refresh the data fork mapping beforehand, which means that the\nxfs_bmap_trim_cow in that function queries the refcount btree about the\nwrong physical blocks and returns an inaccurate value in *shared.\n\nIf *shared is now false, the directio write proceeds with a stale data\nfork mapping.  Fix this by querying the data fork mapping if the\nsequence counter changes across the ILOCK cycle.", "datePublished": "2026-07-23T05:46:56", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T20:48:43", "baseScore": 7.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/dc11be133efca5fe3a2fb02b016dee825cc12f18", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b8c9aa832b52680ee40d6cab0efb081f9a69df05", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/50f0012da1040f69a4e788cd9aed587c9a04983f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e705d81a7193dd19e69b8e2bad4696d78a4ea075", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/206c09b04dc5469c7ff14d8aceff2d47c88078d9", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/44f891bc088958399eec27f7604928694aa35581", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2f4acd0fcd862e22eab45690ec2c08c80b6ef2e7", "https://cdn2.qualys.com/advisory/2026/07/22/RefluXFS.txt"], "aliases": ["GHSA-6p99-w6f4-qcvq", "CVE-2026-64600"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.47, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0b1f3812-57d4-307f-973e-0180f12c1f4e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.1.4"}, {"id": "0f4e2532-920b-3fa9-8578-8b47c5338da6", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "3c68d44a2b49a0ac9165faa9c191e1e618c8a8d5 <50f0012da1040f69a4e788cd9aed587c9a04983f"}, {"id": "10a9a1d6-ecf8-311d-8077-e5e228902aeb", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.15.212"}, {"id": "2ae3f82d-0b83-34d6-b7c3-d7b476497e84", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "3c68d44a2b49a0ac9165faa9c191e1e618c8a8d5 <dc11be133efca5fe3a2fb02b016dee825cc12f18"}, {"id": "55f0fd30-d8c1-37cd-b8ba-2fddbbb33214", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.145"}, {"id": "6a8fa02d-f702-3140-87fc-642ffd92b802", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "3c68d44a2b49a0ac9165faa9c191e1e618c8a8d5 <2f4acd0fcd862e22eab45690ec2c08c80b6ef2e7"}, {"id": "8e752b6b-0ddc-31cb-816a-326dc6b9386b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.1.178"}, {"id": "920476d5-fc8c-3ea0-bddb-1952f573c789", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.39"}, {"id": "94650bfc-4713-31fb-8171-062627eb65e2", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2"}, {"id": "951e75b6-d6d5-339c-8a5d-beb9742047f8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "3c68d44a2b49a0ac9165faa9c191e1e618c8a8d5 <44f891bc088958399eec27f7604928694aa35581"}, {"id": "adf91507-049a-35fc-8473-0f9c107118b6", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "3c68d44a2b49a0ac9165faa9c191e1e618c8a8d5 <b8c9aa832b52680ee40d6cab0efb081f9a69df05"}, {"id": "b14a0daf-c0f8-3072-bdbd-7ba318ce4992", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "3c68d44a2b49a0ac9165faa9c191e1e618c8a8d5 <e705d81a7193dd19e69b8e